Even if you have an aversion to furries, this is a game worth playing through. I held off on picking it up for that exact reason until it was included in a humble bundle I was purchasing for other, less memorable games. While the characters are pretty threadbare tropes (
), and the cutscenes are positively cringe-inducing, those are the only real negatives. This is a solid metroidvania style action platformer with a decent combat system, tight controls, regular crafting upgrades for your gear, and new abilities unlocked every story mission. Collecting all the hidden treasures and rescuing "friends" (
) gave me a solid 15 hours of satisfying play.

Yeah this game is for those that liked old games from the past with a twist. The game plays like a old Space Invaders but has a twist with Platform mechanics . The game is very Bullet Hell and can be very challenging. The game has very old school vibrant look and runs pretty slick. The games soundtrack is good enuf to enjoy as you play. The Boss Battles are pretty neat and challenging also with so much going on!
I say if you like old school arcade shooters pick this one up !
{{Side note also the DEV is a really nice guy and im sure if thier is any issues with the game im sure he will address it ASAP.}}

I really liked it! Cool low poly graphics, nice puzzles and overall a great game!
The music is also pretty nice so it makes you want to play just a lilttle more :)
